@inject Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.IConfiguration Configuration
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <link rel="icon" href="data:," />
    <title>Active translation — Tag Helpers, View Components &amp; HTMX 4</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css/demo.css" />
    <script src="~/lib/htmx/htmx.min.js" defer></script>
    <script src="~/lib/signalr/signalr.min.js" defer></script>
    <script src="~/_content/mostlylucid.activetranslatetag/js/active-translation.js"
            data-active-translation-hub="@Url.Content("~/_active-translate/hub")" defer></script>
</head>
<body>
<main>
    <p class="eyebrow">ASP.NET Core tutorial · HTMX 4</p>
    <h1>Content that translates<br />when it’s ready.</h1>
    <p class="intro">A Tag Helper renders the original message. A local LLM works in the background.
        SignalR announces availability, then HTMX fetches and swaps that one fragment.</p>
    <p class="provider">Provider: <strong>@Configuration["Translation:Provider"]</strong>
        @if (Configuration["Translation:Provider"] == "Sample")
        { <span>— fixed French examples; no model is running.</span> }
    </p>
    <vc:active-translation-status></vc:active-translation-status>
    <section class="posts" aria-label="Forum messages translated into French">
        <article>
            <p class="author">Alex · Original: English → French</p>
            <active-translate language="fr" description="A friendly public forum greeting">
                <h2>Hello, forum!</h2><p>This post translates when the server is ready.</p>
            </active-translate>
        </article>
        <article>
            <p class="author">Sam · Markup and placeholders stay intact</p>
            <active-translate language="fr" description="A forum welcome with a named placeholder and a help link">
                <p>Welcome, {name}.</p><p>Read the <a href="https://www.mostlylucid.net">forum guide</a>.</p>
            </active-translate>
        </article>
        <article>
            <p class="author">Same content, a second location · One inference, two swaps</p>
            <active-translate language="fr" description="A friendly public forum greeting">
                <h2>Hello, forum!</h2><p>This post translates when the server is ready.</p>
            </active-translate>
        </article>
    </section>
    <section class="lesson">
        <h2>One tag, an active fragment</h2>
        <pre><code>&lt;active-translate language="fr" description="A forum message"&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;@@Model.Message&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/active-translate&gt;</code></pre>
        <p>Razor encodes the message. The helper preserves the surrounding HTML, creates a content key,
            and emits <code>hx-get</code>, <code>hx-trigger="translation-ready"</code>, and <code>hx-swap="innerHTML"</code>.</p>
        <p>SQLite keeps completed translations across restarts. Refresh this page after completion to see a cache hit.
            Add <code>mode="server"</code> to await translation before sending the HTML.</p>
    </section>
</main>
</body>
</html>
